 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "grid is a list of equal-length rows over U, P, . and X with exactly one U. Each minute you move to an orthogonally adjacent cell that is not X, and the threat spreads from every threatened cell to its adjacent non-X cells (P cells are threatened at minute 0). A cell is threatened from minute T(c), its breadth-first distance from the nearest P through non-X cells. You may be in cell c at minute t only if t < T(c) (a tie catches you). Return the fewest minutes after which you stand on a border cell (0 when U is on the border), or -1 if impossible.",
  "provenance": [
